## Modules Implemented

| Module | Key Features |
|--------|-------------|
| **National Dashboard** | KPI strip, ICU heatmap, incident board, referral queue, fleet status |
| **Bed & Capacity** | Visual bed grid with vent tags, per-unit snapshot, facility selector |
| **Referral Engine** | SLA timers, accept/decline/escalate actions, audit trail |
| **EMT & Ambulance** | Leaflet live map, field case vitals, dispatch form |
| **Vitals Monitor** | ECG waveforms, live vital fluctuation, critical banners |
| **Telemedicine** | Live video UI, patient context, specialist matching |
| **HECU Dashboard** | ED flow board, on-call registry, critical services |
| **Equipment & NHIMMS** | Registry, fault reports, maintenance calendar |
| **Surge & Disaster** | Incident board, surge activation, mass casualty triage |
| **Analytics & QI** | 8 KPI cards, 4 Chart.js charts, facility scorecards |
| **Clinical Governance** | Trauma/stroke/maternal registries, M&M review queue |
| **Public Interface** | Emergency numbers, hospital finder, first aid guide |
| **Settings & Admin** | User management, role matrix, audit log |

---

## Bugs Fixed

### Bug 1 — Chart.defaults top-level crash
[app.js](file:///c:/laragon/www/nobed/assets/js/app.js) had `Chart.defaults.color = ...` at the top level, which crashed silently when Chart.js CDN hadn't finished executing yet — halting the entire bootstrap (clock showed `--:--`, content area blank, no console errors).

**Fix:** Moved all `Chart.defaults` initialization inside [initApp()](file:///c:/laragon/www/nobed/assets/js/app.js#26-48) with a `window.Chart` guard.

### Bug 2 — Eager function references in PAGES object  
`PAGES.render` used direct references like `render: renderDashboard` — but [app.js](file:///c:/laragon/www/nobed/assets/js/app.js) is loaded before the module scripts, so those functions were `undefined` at parse time.

**Fix:** Wrapped each in a lazy arrow function: `render: (c) => renderDashboard(c)`.

